* Where to Go from here...


The
[[⟪GTI18N_45ef131e_000001⟫][⟪GTI18N_45ef131e_000002⟫ Documentation]] is a great place to
start.
It contains references, tutorials, videos, and more.

To learn how to organize and work with ⟪GTI18N_45ef131e_000003⟫ code, read [[⟪GTI18N_45ef131e_000004⟫][How to Write ⟪GTI18N_45ef131e_000005⟫ Code]].

If you need help with the standard library, see the [[⟪GTI18N_45ef131e_000006⟫][package reference]]. For help with the language itself, you might be surprised to find the [[⟪GTI18N_45ef131e_000007⟫][Language Spec]] is quite readable.

To further explore ⟪GTI18N_45ef131e_000008⟫'s concurrency model, watch
[[⟪GTI18N_45ef131e_000009⟫][⟪GTI18N_45ef131e_000010⟫ Concurrency Patterns]]
([[⟪GTI18N_45ef131e_000011⟫][slides]])
and
[[⟪GTI18N_45ef131e_000012⟫][Advanced ⟪GTI18N_45ef131e_000013⟫ Concurrency Patterns]]
([[⟪GTI18N_45ef131e_000014⟫][slides]])
and read the
[[⟪GTI18N_45ef131e_000015⟫][Share Memory by Communicating]]
codewalk.

To get started writing web applications, watch
[[⟪GTI18N_45ef131e_000016⟫][A simple programming environment]]
([[⟪GTI18N_45ef131e_000017⟫][slides]])
and read the
[[⟪GTI18N_45ef131e_000018⟫][Writing Web Applications]] tutorial.

The [[⟪GTI18N_45ef131e_000019⟫][First Class Functions in ⟪GTI18N_45ef131e_000020⟫]] codewalk gives an interesting perspective on ⟪GTI18N_45ef131e_000021⟫'s function types.

The [[⟪GTI18N_45ef131e_000022⟫][⟪GTI18N_45ef131e_000023⟫ Blog]] has a large archive of informative ⟪GTI18N_45ef131e_000024⟫ articles.

Visit [[⟪GTI18N_45ef131e_000025⟫][the ⟪GTI18N_45ef131e_000026⟫ home page]] for more.
